  "attestation": "D-133 closed-loop round 5 fixes on needs-wording (audit of a888103: 1 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 2 LOW), each narrow and fail-safe. HIGH-1: needsContext keys adopts by the registered text as well (its current holders), and boundUnits of an unasked edit always keeps the unit itself, so a removal binds whatever holds the removed words now: seen {ref: absent} fails once any unit holds them again (the lineage case), and Keep it removed is asked again, never adopting that unit. MEDIUM-2: asksChange returns false for a said answer, so words on a disputed claim never become an instructor-change-owed. MEDIUM-3: owedWords (saidOwed matched to the host-answer marker) is returned by every apply (owed) and export (owedToYou in the CLI), and by coursewerk.mjs status (owedWords); alembic-job/CLAUDE.md says to take each up at the start of every job. MEDIUM-5: taken-up records binding: true for a binding kind (or an unknown kind, fail-safe; the marker now carries the kind) and answeredBases does not count such words as the answer, so the question is asked again with its choices. LOW-4: taken-up resolves the owed words from the log (owedWords), not the needs record, so a pruned hand-in can still be taken up. LOW-6: an answer skipped by the passage check is marked once (host-answer, outcome asked again), so later applies report it already recorded. Probes adopted unchanged as tests/needs-wording.audit5.test.mjs, registered for req.host.alembic-needs-wording and req.host.alembic-needs-apply (statement records round 5). CHANGELOG Unreleased updated; VERSION unchanged. Reviewed every required item. Tests, the full suite: the 36 required plus alembic-needs, alembic-needs-wording, needs-wording audits 1-5, job-release, verdict-path, d49-decisions and all 27 red-team suites: 963 passed, 0 failed (COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed, concurrency 2, one test process under the shared lock).",
